# Platform Auth

This repository contains the code for the Platform Auth Nginx ingress controller.

## Building and Running

The following should work for a standard Kubernetes installation:

```bash
helm fetch --untar https://raw.githubusercontent.com/platform-operator/charts/master/helm/platform-auth
cd platform-auth
sed -i.bak 's/{{ version }}/v1/g' values.yaml
make docker-build push all
```

The above commands will build, push, and deploy a container image named `platform/auth:v1`, which should be available at `nginx.platform.auth`.

You can also use `kubectl apply -f <path-to-chart>` to install the chart locally using kubectl, though you probably want to create an admin user first if there are no users currently created on the cluster.

## Usage

By default, the platform auth configmap sets up a single, public-facing ingress rule with a hostname of `auth.example.com`. This is only useful when testing locally; the production configmaps set up a private cluster IP, which is how the auth components interact with the rest of the platform via API calls.

The platform auth configmap uses the Nginx configuration template provided by the nginx-ingress project (specifically, see the `templates/default.conf.template`) and adds some specific flags for our usage. See the [Nginx documentation](https://github.com/kubernetes/ingress-nginx/blob/main/docs/user-guide/nginx-configuration/configmap.md) for details on these flags.

For example, here's what the public-facing config might look like:

```yaml
apiVersion: extensions/v1beta1
kind: ConfigMap
metadata:
  name: nginx-ingress
  namespace: default
data:
  env: |-
    AUTH_HOST=auth.example.com
    AUTH_API_URL=https://{{ .Release.Name }}-webapps.auth.example.com/
    AUTH_ADMIN_LOGIN=admin
    AUTH_ADMIN_PASSWORD=password
  nginx.ingress.kubernetes.io/auth-tls-secret: auth-public
  nginx.ingress.kubernetes.io/auth-tls-verify-client: off
  nginx.ingress.kubernetes.io/auth-url: https://auth.example.com/api/login/oauth/token
  nginx.ingress.kubernetes.io/client-body-buffer-size: 1m
  nginx.ingress.kubernetes.io/proxy-connect-timeout: '10'
  nginx.ingress.kubernetes.io/proxy-read-timeout: '10'
  nginx.ingress.kubernetes.io/proxy-send-timeout: '10'
  nginx.ingress.kubernetes.io/server-snippet: |
    location / {
      proxy_http_version 1.1;
      proxy_set_header Upgrade $http_upgrade;
      proxy_set_header Connection keep-alive;
      proxy_set_header Host $host;
      proxy_cache_bypass $http_upgrade;
      client_max_body_size 0;
    }
```

